<p>I initially downvoted the first revision of this article, but have changed my vote to an upvote. It has a few problems (like why Taured itself isn't considered anomalous), but I found myself feeling so very fucking sorry for someone as lost as -1. From his point of view, <em>this</em> is the fucked up anomalous world. And yes, it's been explored in other articles, and this may not be the most perfect execution, but if you make me feel sorry and I want to keep reading, you get an upvote.</p>
<p>One thing though:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The passport contains stamps from airports located in Paris, Taured, Tokyo, The United States of America, and Germany, these stamps match the ones used by the associated country.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sentence sounds off, since Taured isn't recognized as a country and thus doesn't have a stamp recognized in this reality construct to match it against. Maybe change to:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The passport contains stamps from airports located in Paris, Tokyo, The United States of America, and Germany, matching the ones used by the associated country. It also contains a stamp for the Taured National Airport.</p>
</blockquote>

